      "score": 1,
      "reason": "It includes adoption, impact, investment, market-sizing, and bubble-risk data bearing on health and direction.",
      "report_quote": "88% of organizations regularly use AI in at least one business function (up from 78% a year earlier), and 62% are at least experimenting with AI agents — but only ~one-third have begun scaling AI programs, and just 39% report enterprise-level EBIT impact"
    },
    {
      "id": "C6",
      "score": 1,
      "reason": "It flags regulatory fragmentation, privacy regimes, multilateral economic forums, macro/bubble risk, and labor scrutiny; one UNCTAD16 item is dated/past rather than upcoming, but the flagging function is met.",
      "report_quote": "**Fragmented global AI regulation is the headline risk.** No country has comprehensive AI regulation yet; approaches diverge"
    }
  ],
  "sampled_claims": [
    {
      "report_quote": "88% of organizations regularly use AI in at least one business function (up from 78% a year earlier), and 62% are at least experimenting with AI agents — but only ~one-third have begun scaling AI programs, and just 39% report enterprise-level EBIT impact",
      "source_id": "D0074",
      "source_quote": "88 percent report regular AI use in at least one business function, compared with 78 percent a year ago. But at the enterprise level, the majority are still in the experimenting or piloting stages ... approximately one-third reporting that their companies have begun to scale their AI programs.",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "reason": "D0074 contains the 88/78 figures, one-third scaling, 62% agent experimentation, and 39% enterprise EBIT impact."
    },
    {
      "report_quote": "your model assumes smooth revenue growth to $14.9M by 2028 with a stable ~74% gross margin, zero taxes, and no additional financing after 2024.",
      "source_id": "user_file:prediction.csv",
      "source_quote": "2028,Total Revenue,3350000,3600000,3850000,4100000,14900000\n2028,Gross Margin,\"73.9%\",\"73.9%\",\"73.9%\",\"73.9%\",\"73.9%\"\n2028,Taxes,0,0,0,0,0\n2025,Cash Flow from Financing,0,0,0,0,0\n2026,Cash Flow from Financing,0,0,0,0,0\n2027,Cash Flow from Financing,0,0,0,0,0\n2028,Cash Flow from Financing,0,0,0,0,0",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "reason": "The CSV shows 2028 revenue of 14,900,000, annual gross margin 73.9%, taxes of 0 across years, and financing cash flows of 0 after the 2024 $1,000,000 inflow."
    },
    {
      "report_quote": "Double-digit CAGRs are the norm across the syndicated reports sampled (D0013, D0125, D0138, D0188)",
      "source_id": "D0125;D0188;D0138",
      "source_quote": "D0188: \"projected to grow at a CAGR of 7.7%\"; \"CAGR of 9.9%\"; \"CAGR of 3.6%\"; \"CAGR of 4.7%\". D0125: \"growing at a CAGR of 7.1%\"; \"growing at a CAGR of 6.2%\"; \"growing at a CAGR of 5.7%\"; \"growing at a CAGR of 3.5%\". D0138: \"CAGR of 15.3%\" but also \"CAGR of 9.1%\", \"CAGR of 7.2%\", \"CAGR of 5.4%\", \"CAGR of 6.3%\".",
      "verdict": "contradicted",
      "reason": "The cited syndicated listings include many single-digit CAGRs, especially in consumer goods, chemicals, and agrochemicals; double-digit growth appears common in some tech listings but is not the norm across the sampled set."
    },
    {
      "report_quote": "the Stargate project alone pledges $100B initially and up to $500B; Microsoft announced ~$80B for AI data centers in 2025; Nvidia committed up to $100B to OpenAI contingent on OpenAI buying Nvidia capacity",
      "source_id": "D0167",
      "source_quote": "pledging $100 billion to start, with plans to invest up to $500 billion into Stargate in the coming years. Nvidia GPUs would be deployed.",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "reason": "D0167 supports Stargate's $100B/$500B pledge, Microsoft's approximately $80B 2025 data-center plan, and Nvidia's up-to-$100B OpenAI investment conditioned on OpenAI using Nvidia systems."
    },
    {
      "report_quote": "No country has comprehensive AI regulation yet; approaches diverge — broad horizontal regulation (EU, South Korea), sector-specific rules (US), and principles/guidelines (Brazil, Singapore, US).",
      "source_id": "D0148",
      "source_quote": "While no country has passed comprehensive AI or gen AI regulation to date, leading legislative efforts include those in Brazil, China, the European Union, Singapore, South Korea, and the United States.",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "reason": "D0148 explicitly states the no-comprehensive-regulation claim and the same divergent approaches; the report itself separately warns this may be time-sensitive/stale, but the supplied source supports the sentence."
    }
  ]
